{"name":"Hawk’s Eye","hex":"#34363a","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"hawk","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A diurnal predatory bird of the family Accipitridae, smaller than an eagle.","Any diurnal predatory terrestrial bird of similar size and appearance to the accipitrid hawks, such as a falcon."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To hunt with a hawk.","To make an attack while on the wing; to soar and strike like a hawk."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/hawk"},{"term":"eye","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["An organ through which animals see (“perceive surroundings via light”).","The visual sense."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To carefully or appraisingly observe (someone or something).","To consider."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/eye"}],"entries":[{"title":"Tiger's eye","blocks":[{"text":"Tiger's eye is a\nchatoyant gemstone that is usually a metamorphic rock with a golden to red-brown colour and a silky lustre. As members of the quartz group, tiger's eye and the related blue-coloured mineral hawk's eye gain their silky, lustrous appearance from the parallel intergrowth of quartz crystals and altered amphibole fibres that have mostly turned into limonite."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/be/Tiger%27s_eye.jpg/330px-Tiger%27s_eye.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tiger's_eye","wikidata":"Q430007"},{"title":"Eye","blocks":[{"text":"An eye is a sensory organ that allows an organism to perceive visual information. It detects light and converts it into electro-chemical impulses in neurons (neurones). It is part of an organism's visual system."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/64/Krilleyekils.jpg/330px-Krilleyekils.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eye","wikidata":"Q7364"},{"title":"Hawk","blocks":[{"text":"Hawks are birds of prey of the family Accipitridae. They are very widely distributed and are found on all continents, except Antarctica."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/81/Northern_Goshawk_ad_M2.jpg/330px-Northern_Goshawk_ad_M2.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hawk","wikidata":"Q846664"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Tiger_iron_slabs.jpg/250px-Tiger_iron_slabs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Tiger_iron_slabs.jpg/500px-Tiger_iron_slabs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/d/d9/Tiger_iron_slabs.jpg/250px-Tiger_iron_slabs.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ATiger_iron_slabs.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Quartz_-_Tigers-Eye_-_raw_stone_from_Southafrica.jpg/330px-Quartz_-_Tigers-Eye_-_raw_stone_from_Southafrica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Quartz_-_Tigers-Eye_-_raw_stone_from_Southafrica.jpg/960px-Quartz_-_Tigers-Eye_-_raw_stone_from_Southafrica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Quartz_-_Tigers-Eye_-_raw_stone_from_Southafrica.jpg/330px-Quartz_-_Tigers-Eye_-_raw_stone_from_Southafrica.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AQuartz_-_Tigers-Eye_-_raw_stone_from_Southafrica.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/7